  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CGIAR: Multilateral Contributions (Portfolio Funding)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The multilateral activities of CGIAR contribute directly to the strategic goals of the Australian aid program, with particular relevance to the Strategy framework for Australia&#x2019;s aid investments in the agriculture, fisheries and water sectors (AFW). CGIAR&#x2019;s focus on gender and inclusive growth aligns well with the framework&#x2019;s recognition that women&#x2019;s economic empowerment is integral to tackling poverty and maximising development outcomes. ACIAR&#x2019;s contribution to CGIAR Portfolio funding allocated through the CGIAR System Council supports CGIAR system costs as a whole. The System Council is the governance and decision-making body of CGIAR represented by donors (including Australia) and other stakeholders, which determines how these funds are allocated to CGIAR, which may include allocation to CGIAR Research Programs (see below), used to pay system costs or otherwise applied to achieving the CGIAR mission.</narrative>
  </description>
